      "id": "33173d895637-q19",
      "number": 19,
      "question": "Six letters A, M, R, S, Y and Q are written on different faces of a dice. Two positions of this dice are shown in the figures below. Find the letter on the face opposite to S.",
      "questionHtml": "Six letters A, M, R, S, Y and Q are written on different faces of a dice. Two positions of this dice are shown in the figures below. Find the letter on the face opposite to S.<br />\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravS_SSC_2_12_24_D119.png\" style=\"width: 164px; height: 85px;\" />",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Q",
          "html": "Q"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "M",
          "html": "M"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Y",
          "html": "Y"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "A",
          "html": "A"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">As R is common on both the dices, it is clear that M, A, Y, and S are adjacent to it, and the remaining i.e. Q will be opposite to it.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravS_SSC_2_12_24_D120.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 178px; height: 95px;\" />​</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Opposite pairs:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">M → Y</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">A → S</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">R → Q</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, the opposite side of \"S\" will be side \"A\".</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravS_SSC_2_12_24_D119.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravS_SSC_2_12_24_D120.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33173d895637-q20",
      "number": 20,
      "question": "Which two numbers (not digits) should be interchanged to make the given equation correct? 24 &divide; 3 &ndash; 4 &times; 2 + 6 &times; 5 +12 = 50",
      "questionHtml": "Which two numbers (not digits) should be interchanged to make the given equation correct?<br />\n24 &divide; 3 &ndash; 4 &times; 2 + 6 &times; 5 +12 = 50",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "5 and 4",
          "html": "5 and 4"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "4 and 3",
          "html": "4 and 3"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "24 and 12",
          "html": "24 and 12"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "3 and 2",
          "html": "3 and 2"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Option  3) 24 and 12</p>\n\n<p>24 ÷ 3 – 4 × 2 + 6 × 5 +12 = 50 ⇒ 12 ÷ 3 – 4 × 2 + 6 × 5 +24 = 50</p>\n\n<p>⇒ 12 ÷ 3 – 4 × 2 + 6 × 5 +24 = 50 ⇒ 4 – 4 × 2 + 6 × 5 +24 = 50 ⇒ 4 + 30 +24 – 8 = 50 ⇒ 58 – 8 = 50 ⇒ 50 = 50 (LHS = RHS)</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33173d895637-q21",
      "number": 21,
      "question": "Six letters P, Q, R, S, T and U are written on different faces of a dice. Two positions of this dice are shown in the figure below. Find the letter on the face opposite to R.",
      "questionHtml": "Six letters P, Q, R, S, T and U are written on different faces of a dice. Two positions of this dice are shown in the figure below. Find the letter on the face opposite to R.<br />\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravA_SSC_2_12_24_D121.png\" style=\"width: 177px; height: 81px;\" />",
      "options": [
