        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "S",
          "html": "S"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">As R is common on both the dices, it is clear that P, T, Q, and U are adjacent to it, and the remaining i.e. S will be opposite to it.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravS_SSC_2_12_24_D122.png\" style=\"width: 228px; height: 91px;\" />​</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Opposite pairs:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">P → Q</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">T → U</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">R → S</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, the opposite side of \"R\" will be side \"S\".</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/12/F1_SouravA_SSC_2_12_24_D121.png",
